{
  "id": "033",
  "title": "Forty-Two and Nine",
  "subtitle": "\"I was forty-two. He was twenty-nine. He was renovating the house I had just bought with the money from my divorce.\"",
  "penName": "Margaux Renn",
  "genre": "ageGap",
  "hook": "I was forty-two years old when I bought a farmhouse in the Catskills with the only thing my ex-husband and I had ever agreed on: that I should keep it. Reid Varney was the carpenter the realtor recommended for the renovation. He was twenty-nine. He wore boots and quiet and the kind of focus that made me notice. He showed up on a Tuesday in September with a clipboard, asked me seven questions about the porch, and left with the estimate. I called him back Wednesday. I did not call him back for the porch.",
